A||N||2||MIKLAV||High Idle V-6||||1
Z||000000||MIKLAV||10-07-1999||12:55 PM||||Ok, thanks for everyone advice dealing with the high idle for my '86 GT.  I believe the problem has been found.  The TBI is leaking outside air into the intake.  From the outside of the TBI, I sprayed a bunch of carb cleaner where the butterfly valve is connected to the throttle cable, where the spring is.  Sure enough the car almost stalled and white smoke came out the exhaust pipes.  I called NAPA but they don't carry any rebuilding kits for the TBI.  Anybody have any suggestions?<BR>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-07-1999||02:05 PM||||I saw one for sale on Ebay, or you could just get one from a salvage yard.  I have never heard of a Fiero throtle body leaking like as you describe, so a used one may be the ideal solution.<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=176986077" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=176986077</A> <P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-07-1999||02:06 PM||||If it was being pulled in around the throttle shaft, the thing needs to be replaced or you need to find a way to get bushings into it. Unfortunatly they don't build this stuff with bushings so it has to be machined for them. not easy work, and requires a level of pressicion difficult to reach without some large machinery.<P>If it's getting in around the shaft, then also likely the TB bore is worn from a missaligned butterfly. That kind of damage can't be fixed. Well it can be but again it requires a machine shop.<P>you might try messing with the idle stop screw on the TB. You may be able to adjust out some of the leak. Ultimatly tho you'll have to replace the thing.||||reg||1
